💡 **SUGGESTION: the sibling `/models config` printer wasn't taught the new slot states**

This hunk fixed the stale pre-gh-1844 label in the settings flow (`_mediaSlotDescription` now renders all four states), but the CLI's other slot printer — `/models config` (`_printModelsConfig`, `lib/src/cli/provider_models.dart:1083-1103`, unchanged in this diff) — still shows the old world, so the same configuration renders inconsistently across the two surfaces:

- header: `media slots (no override = main connection):` — the exact pre-gh-1844 claim this PR corrects elsewhere (no override = UNCONFIGURED, never an inherited main endpoint);
- a `null` override prints `  <slot>: main connection` (same stale label);
- an **unsupported** slot (new state) prints `  musicGeneration:  @ (openai-completions)` — empty model/baseUrl with no hint the capability was removed;
- a `useMainConnection` slot prints the same blank ` @ ` shape (pre-existing, but the new state inherits it).

Suggested: mirror the four-state logic here (or reuse `_mediaSlotDescription`), e.g. header `no override = not configured`, `  <slot>: not configured`, `  <slot>: unsupported (capability removed)`, `  <slot>: main connection`, `  <slot>: <modelId> @ <baseUrl> (openai-completions)`.

Display-only (no tool behavior affected), so suggestion-level — but it is the PR's own stated sweep ("the stale pre-gh-1844 unconfigured label now reads 'not configured'") missing one surface. Anchored here since this is the hunk that introduced the four-state display; the file to touch is outside the diff.

